  <div class="mark-scheme">
    <p class="ms-header">Mark Scheme &mdash; Question 5</p>
    <div class="ms-point"><strong>(a)</strong> M1: Calculate x&sup2; values: 0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 25 cm&sup2;. Plot points (x&sup2;, E<sub>k</sub>): (0,45.0), (1,42.8), (4,36.0), (9,24.5), (16,8.0), (25,0.0). A1: Best-fit straight line drawn with negative gradient. M1: x<sub>0</sub>&sup2; is the x-intercept (where E<sub>k</sub> = 0) &rarr; x<sub>0</sub>&sup2; = 25 cm&sup2; &rarr; x<sub>0</sub> = 5.0 cm. A1: E<sub>k</sub> = &frac12;m&omega;&sup2;(x<sub>0</sub>&sup2; &minus; x&sup2;). Gradient = &minus;&frac12;m&omega;&sup2; = (45.0 &minus; 0)/(0 &minus; 25) = &minus;1.80 mJ cm<sup>&minus;2</sup> = &minus;18 J m<sup>&minus;2</sup>. &omega;&sup2; = 2 &times; |gradient| / m = 2 &times; 18 / 0.050 = 720. &omega; = 26.8 rad s<sup>&minus;1</sup>. [4]</div>
    <div class="ms-point"><strong>(b)</strong> M1: E<sub>total</sub> = E<sub>k</sub>(x=0) = 45.0 mJ (accept 45&ndash;46 mJ). A1: k = m&omega;&sup2; = 0.050 &times; 720 = 36 N m<sup>&minus;1</sup>. (Or: E<sub>total</sub> = &frac12;kx<sub>0</sub>&sup2; &rarr; k = 2E<sub>total</sub>/x<sub>0</sub>&sup2; = 2 &times; 0.045 / 0.05&sup2; = 36 N m<sup>&minus;1</sup>.) [2]</div>
    <div class="ms-point"><strong>(c)</strong> M1: The spring's mass contributes to the inertia but not to the restoring force, so the effective mass is greater than 50 g. A1: Since &omega; = &radic;(k/m<sub>eff</sub>), a larger effective mass means a smaller &omega;. The value calculated ignoring spring mass (26.8 rad s<sup>&minus;1</sup>) would be an <strong>overestimate</strong>. [2]</div>
    <p class="ms-total">Total: [8]</p>
